Package: paco
Version: __VERSION__
Architecture: __ARCH__
Maintainer: Paco Maintainers <noreply@localhost>
Homepage: https://github.com/stack256org/paco
Depends: postgresql, postgresql-client, nginx, git, ca-certificates, adduser, sudo
Recommends: docker.io
Suggests: gh, certbot, python3-certbot-nginx
Description: self-hosted AI coding agent
 Paco drives the Claude Code CLI headlessly and maps its streaming output to
 a web UI, so a team can run their own coding-agent instance instead of a
 hosted one.
 .
 This package installs Paco itself, a bundled Node.js runtime, a bundled
 Claude Code CLI, a systemd service, and an nginx site. Postgres and nginx
 run as ordinary host packages; Docker is used only to run per-chat
 sandboxes, so it is a recommendation rather than a hard dependency — Paco
 starts and serves its UI without it, and an operator with an existing
 Docker setup should not get a second one.
 .
 GitHub's gh CLI is not packaged here (it ships from GitHub's own APT
 repository) but is required before anyone connects a GitHub account; the
 postinst script warns if it is missing.
